  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14272746/assets/d8452e497edc454ac0a71b4b5e9f00308ef7dbeb9c1413cc2bc82bbafb669b04.png)\n\nA chemical is being poured into a conical vat at a constant rate of $18\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/h}.$ The vat has a radius of $10\\,\\text{m}$ at the wider end and a height of $10\\,\\text{m}.$ Find the rate of the liquid level increase at the moment when there is $9\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}$ of liquid in the vat. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe liquid level is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}} $\\text{m}/\\text{h}.$",
